{
  "what": "THE ONE STATEMENT OF WHAT THE OWNERSHIP TREE ANSWERS, read by both languages.",
  "why": [
    "The tree, the descendants, the crew summary and the attention order exist twice: in TypeScript",
    "(packages/client-core/src/sessions/tree.ts, shipped first) and in C#",
    "(src/CcDirector.Gateway.Contracts/SessionTree.cs, ported for the Director rail). Two folds of one",
    "question drift - that is the defect this whole mission exists to stop, so it cannot be the shape of",
    "its own fix.",
    "",
    "So neither implementation owns the answer: this file does. tree.agreement.test.ts runs the",
    "TypeScript fold over these sessions and asserts these answers; TreeAgreementTests runs the C# fold",
    "over the same sessions and asserts the same answers, and CcDirector.StateAgreementCheck runs it",
    "again on every run of the live check. Change either fold on its own and that language goes red;",
    "change a fold AND this file together and the OTHER language goes red. There is no way to move one",
    "side quietly.",
    "",
    "EACH SESSION CARRIES BOTH ITS RAW FACTS AND THE GATEWAY'S STAMP, because the two folds take",
    "different input: the browser reads the stamped triageBucket, while the C# calls",
    "SessionOrdering.Classify and folds the same answer from activityState, onHold and",
    "hasLiveSupervisor. The C# checker asserts, per session, that the fold it computes equals the stamp",
    "written here - so a fixture that quietly says two different things about one session is itself a",
    "finding, and the bridge between the two languages is checked rather than assumed."
  ],
  "descendantFormat": "sessionId@directParentId@depth, depth relative to the root it was asked about",
  "cases": [
